COMPLETED: Video in the video section has been made 30% smaller while maintaining aspect ratio. The changes have been applied to the custom-additions.css file.

ADDITIONAL CHANGE (2025-04-11):
- Updated the CSS to reduce both the container AND the video by 30% 
- Modified the custom-additions.css file with the following changes:
  ```css
  /* Make the video in the video section 30% smaller */
  .project[data-category="video"] .device-mockup {
      width: 70%; /* Reduced by 30% from original size */
      margin: 0 auto;
      transform: scale(0.7); /* Additional 30% reduction in overall size */
      transform-origin: center center;
  }

  .project[data-category="video"] .device-mockup video.video-portrait {
      width: 100%; /* Fill the container */
      height: auto;
      display: block;
  }
  ```
- This applies a double reduction: first setting width to 70% and then applying a scale transform of 0.7 (70%)
- The result is that both the container and video are significantly reduced in size

ADDITIONAL CHANGE (2025-04-11):
- Reduced the height of the design project section to make it look neater
- Modified the custom-additions.css file with the following changes:
  ```css
  /* Custom styling for the Graphic Design project image */
  .project[data-category="design"] {
      padding: 2rem; /* Reduce padding from default 3rem */
  }

  .project[data-category="design"] .device-mockup {
      max-width: 75%; /* Reduced from 100% */
      margin: 0 auto; /* Center the container */
      max-height: 350px; /* Limit maximum height */
      overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Preserve aspect ratio */
  .project[data-category="design"] .device-mockup img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      object-fit: contain;
      max-height: 100%;
  }

  /* Make the content section more compact */
  .project[data-category="design"] .project-content {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.75rem; /* Reduced spacing between elements */
  }

  .project[data-category="design"] .project-content p {
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem; /* Reduced margin */
  }
  ```
- These changes make the design project section more compact by:
  1. Reducing the overall padding of the section
  2. Limiting the maximum height of the image container
  3. Making the text content more compact with reduced spacing

